speechtext:
I have the figures here for the prosecutions in connection with cigarette seizures and motor vehicles seized and sold, if those are the prosecutions to which the hon. gentleman refers. We have a series of them. These are the cigarette seizures; in 1950, 254; 1951, 558; 1952, 813; 1953, 378;
1954,	175; 1955, the same figure, 175; 1956, 134; 1957, 76. Now, the number of prosecutions does not always follow exactly the number of seizures. It is slightly less. The prosecutions, for instance, in 1950 were 242; in 1951, 535; 1952, 779; 1953, 350; 1954, 167;
1955,	165; 1956, 127; 1957, 72.
Motor vehicles seized and forfeited for the same years are as follows: 52, 184, 260, 78, 50, 26, 22 and 19.
